        "explanation": "Let \\(y=x^{2}\\). Then \\(y^{2}-2(k+1)y+k^{2}-1=0\\), giving \\(y=k+1\\pm\\sqrt{2(k+1)}\\). For four distinct real values of \\(x\\), both distinct \\(y\\)-values must be positive. The smaller one is positive exactly when \\(k+1>\\sqrt{2(k+1)}\\), which gives \\(k>1\\).",
